.TH "libnvmf_config_conn_get_transport" 9 "libnvmf_config_conn_get_transport" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_config_conn_get_transport \- a connection's transport.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "const char *" libnvmf_config_conn_get_transport
.BI "(const struct libnvmf_config_conn *conn "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "conn" 12
the resolved connection
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Addressing is exposed as raw strings, not a TID: the configuration is a
human interface and traddr/host-traddr may legitimately name a host,
while TID construction rejects one.  Resolve first, then build a TID
with \fBlibnvmf_tid_from_fields\fP + \fBlibnvmf_tid_set_identity\fP.
.SH "RETURN"
borrowed string, valid while the owning configuration is alive.
